
The Bolognese Biance (White variation)

Are you sure this is the best title ^

This version skips the tomato entirely, focusing on the richness of the meat, cream, and herbs. It’s decadent and feels a bit more "gourmet."

The Twist
The Sauce Base: Instead of tomato, use a mix of 1/2 cup ricotta and 1 tbsp heavy cream seasoned with garlic powder and nutmeg.

The Meat: Cook the Bolognese as before, but skip the tomato paste. Use white wine (Pinot Grigio) instead of red.

The Toppings:

Fresh mozzarella (fior di latte).

A handful of sautéed mushrooms.

Finish: A drizzle of truffle oil and fresh parsley.

Quick How-To
Brown your meat with the aromatics (onion/garlic) and deglaze with white wine. Add a splash of milk and simmer until dry.

Spread the ricotta mixture onto the dough.

Add the white meat sauce and mushrooms.

Bake until the edges are golden and the ricotta is set.

2. The "Zing" Bolognese (Spicy & Tangy)
This is for when you want the comfort of a meat sauce but need it to wake up your taste buds. It leans into acidity and heat to cut through the fat of the beef and pork.

The Twist
The Sauce Base: Your standard thick Bolognese from the first recipe, but add 1 tsp red pepper flakes and 1 tsp smoked paprika during the browning stage.

The Toppings:

Pickled Elements: Sliced pickled jalapeños or pepperoncini.

Red Onion: Thinly shaved red onions (they caramelize beautifully in the high heat).

Cheese: Mix mozzarella with a little Sharp Provolone for extra bite.

The Finish: A drizzle of Hot Honey or a squeeze of fresh lime right before serving.

Quick How-To
Prepare the "Extra Thick" Ragù with the added spices.

Layer the dough with a thin layer of spicy marinara or the meat sauce directly.

Load up on the onions and pickled peppers.

Bake until the crust is charred. The contrast between the heavy meat and the vinegary peppers is the star here.

Which "Vibe" are you going for?
Bianca: Best paired with a cold glass of white wine and a fancy movie night.

Zing: Best paired with a cold beer and a Sunday football game.

